...
Mike> Even worse is the fact that some numbers, like \arraystretch
Mike> *have* to be set as commands, rather than assigned to.

This is bad, but it is not really LaTeX's fault. \arraystretch is not
a <number> it is a <factor> and TeX does not provide any type of
registers or arithmetic for `real' numbers. You can just use them in
certain very specific places for multiplying dimen registers.

It would of course be posible to `fake' fixed point numbers with
dimen registers, eg as done by the calc package.

David

